Ask a chief information security officer a simple question: *"Would you allow a software process whose control flow can be rewritten by an untrusted paragraph inside an incoming customer PDF to hold write credentials to our ERP?"*

Every CISO on earth will say no in less than a second.

Yet that is the exact architecture of most first-generation AI agents. When a single runtime process ingests untrusted text, decides which tool to call, and holds static OAuth or API keys to downstream business systems, **every document becomes executable code**.

{% callout tone="warning" title="System Prompts Are Advice, Not Security Boundaries" %}
Telling a language model *"Never call payroll endpoints unless the user is an HR director"* inside a system prompt is equivalent to enforcing enterprise authorization in client-side JavaScript. Security must live in deterministic services outside the model's token stream.
{% /callout %}

